	(text "USB-C 5 V CHARGE PORT - CH224K PD SINK, 5 V ONLY (higher-voltage PD charging deferred)\nPurpose: lets modern USB-C chargers supply more current at 5 V (explicit 5 V PD contract) for the 3x TP4056 chargers.\n5 V ONLY: CFG1 (pin 9) tied directly to VDD = level mode CFG1=1 -> 5 V request. CFG2/CFG3 to GND.\nDO NOT fit a resistor on CFG1 and do not leave it open: resistor / open CFG1 selects 9/12/15/20 V.\nPD-only mode (CH224 datasheet 5.5): DP shorted to DM on the CH224K, not wired to the connector.\nCH224K has internal Rd on CC1/CC2 (no external 5.1k). VBUS_C -> D55 SS34 -> +5V, in parallel with micro-B inputs D8/D9."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
